"""Synthetic cases for study 04: what a sentence-level checker sees.

Each case is one piece of agent output (an email reply, a client update, a
short research brief or a meeting follow-up) together with the records the
agent read through its tools before writing it. The records are split in two:

- ``cited``: what the output cites or replies to (the email thread, the fetched
  page, the meeting notes). In the production system this was all the checker
  was given.
- ``other``: everything else the agent read: CRM fields, internal notes,
  earlier threads, calendar lookups and other tool results (including failed
  fetches such as an HTTP 403). Some of these are distractors that no output
  sentence uses.

The output is already split into sentences, one per item, in order. Each
sentence carries a label:

- ``cited``: stated in or directly supported by a cited record (``basis``).
- ``other``: supported by an ``other`` record and not by any cited record
  (``basis``). A sentence that needs an ``other`` record for any part of what
  it says is labelled ``other``.
- ``unsupported``: a factual claim no record supports (a planted error).
- ``contradicted``: a factual claim a record contradicts (a planted error;
  ``basis`` names that record, cited or other).
- ``not_a_claim``: greetings, sign-offs, questions and offers with no factual
  content.

Planted errors also carry ``error``: wrong_date, wrong_number, invented_price,
invented_promise, wrong_person, reversed_fact or claim_not_made.

Everything is invented: the firm (Larkspur Advisory, larkspur.example), its
people, every client, prospect, person, product, price and place. All domains
end in ``.example``. The labels are the author's intent, written on 2026-11-15
together with the cases; they were not independently relabelled and no model
under test was consulted.

Split rule: case cNN is in the development split when NN is even (c02, c04,
..., c48) and held out when NN is odd. Thresholds are fitted on the
development split only; reported numbers come from the held-out split.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

