            {"id": "c32-s1", "kind": "web_page", "text": "https://www.halvorsenmarine.example/news/expansion\nHalvorsen Marine Engines will add a second assembly line at its Saltby plant in 2027, creating about 60 jobs. President Erik Halvorsen said demand for its inboard diesel engines had 'outrun our capacity for three years'. The $14 million expansion is supported by a $1.5 million state manufacturing grant, and construction begins in spring 2027. The company currently employs 230 people and builds around 1,900 engines a year, about a third of them for export. Halvorsen engines power fishing boats, ferries and workboats."},
